  "investigation_summary": {
    "root_cause_0_36ms_latency": "The 0.36ms latency reported in historical ablation runs was an artifact of two conditions: (1) QueryEmbeddingCache had already cached query embeddings during preceding Pipeline A execution, reducing 5.57ms FastEmbed ONNX embedding inference to a ~0.001ms in-memory dictionary lookup. (2) LOW_MEMORY_RAG_MODE=True and ENABLE_FLASHRANK=False caused NeuralReranker to operate in degraded passthrough mode ('return candidates[:limit]'), which bypassed cross-encoder inference entirely. Thus, 0.36ms measured only cached in-memory Qdrant + BM25 + slice passthrough, NOT neural retrieval.",
    "hit_at_1_discrepancy_explanation": "The 93.33% Hit@1 on the 30-query dataset (eval_retrieval.py) vs 85.56% Hit@1 on the 100-query hardened dataset (eval_rag_ablations.py) is due to dataset construction: the 30-query corpus consists of exact phrasing and small target documents, whereas the 100-query corpus includes challenging subsets: terminology mismatch (80.0% Hit@1), ambiguous queries (30.0% Hit@1), and adversarial distractors.",
    "historical_88_89_explanation": "The historical 88.89% Hit@1 originated from an early 18-query prototype dataset (16/18 hits), which is mathematically incomparable to both the 30-query and 100-query benchmark sets."
